{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And YHWH appeared to him — how? In that three men came to him, who were angels, for in many places when an angel appears Scripture calls it by the language of the Shekhinah, as written: כי שמי בקרבו — His emissary is like Him. And likewise: וירא מלאך ה׳ אליו בלבת אש מתוך הסנה. And it is written there: וירא ה׳ כי סר לראות." "In the heat of the day — what need is there to write 'היום'? Rather, to inform you that regarding Lot it is written: ויבאו המלאכים סדומה בערב, and therefore Lot said to them: סורו נא אל בית עבדכם ולינו. But Abraham — since they came to him כחם היום in the morning, for it is not the way of travelers to lodge overnight but to eat and move on — therefore he did not tell them to lodge but only: וסעדו לבכם ואחר תעבורו."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:24.503943729Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}